# core_node deletion safety (mandatory)

Never remove, recursively delete, overwrite, or re-clone over the `core_node`
project directory (`$CORE_NODE_DIR` / `$CORE_NODE_PROJECT_ROOT` / `$CORE_NODE_ROOT_DIR`
/ any `*/core_node`) without a guarded **triple confirmation** — each prompt `[N/y]`,
**default N**.

Hard-refuse, with no prompt:
- system/critical paths (`/`, `/usr*`, `/etc*`, `/bin*`, `/sbin*`, `/lib*`, `/var*`, `/home`, `/root`, `/opt`, `/mnt`, `/www*`);
- any **git working tree** (`<target>/.git` exists);
- self-deletion (the dir the process runs from);
- **any non-interactive run** (no TTY → default N → never delete).

An existing populated / `.git` project tree is **authoritative**: a "partial /
incomplete clone" check must **adopt or abort — never delete**.

Use the shared guard `confirm_core_node_deletion` (`scripts/shells/linux/common/gvar_common.sh`,
`scripts/shells/linux/install_bootstrap.sh`). Canonical spec:
`development-guides/CORE_NODE_DELETION_SAFETY.md`.
